nth highs in late August, suggesting institutional interest\n\n  * Enterprise partnerships with major banks and government agencies continue accumulating\n\n  * CCIP expansion to new blockchains like TON and World Chain creates new revenue opportunities\n\nHeadwinds:\n\n  * Macroeconomic concerns including trade war tensions and global economic uncertainty weigh on risk assets\n\n  * Bitcoin price volatility affects overall cryptocurrency market sentiment and risk appetite\n\n  * Competing oracle solutions gain market share in specific niches\n\n  * Staking dilution from new token emissions continues (though decreasing over time)\n\nMarket Psychology: LINK has faced \"altcoin fatigue\" – a phenomenon where capital flows primarily to Bitcoin and Ethereum while alternative tokens struggle. Breaking above $25 resistance levels would likely trigger sustained buying, while falling below $12 would signal bearish reversal.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nExplore · ArXivSignals (https://arxivsignals.io/explore?date=2025-11-04&labs=fudan)\nciteturn2268search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; 2511.01059 2025-11-04 55/100 new-method## Efficient Test-Time Retrieval Augmented Generation\n\nimage-classificationimage-segmentationmedical-image-analysis\n\n[Button: ⧉ link][Button: ⧉ title][Button: ⧉ summary]arXiv ↗\n\n2511.01295 2025-11-04 65/100 benchmark\n\n## UniREditBench: A Unified Reasoning-based Image Editing Benchmark\n\nA reasoning-focused image editing benchmark with a synthetic dataset and fine-tuned model for complex editing tasks.\n\ncomputer-visiongenerative-modelsllm-reasoningmodel-evaluation\n\n[Button: ⧉ link][Button: ⧉ title][Button: ⧉ summary]arXiv ↗\n\n2511.01059 2025-11-04 55/100 new-method\n\n## Efficient Test-Time Retrieval Augmented Generation\n\nA training-free RAG framework using partial generation and majority voting to balance performance and computational cost.\n\ninfer